WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.480
Would Will Smith need to be de-aged, or is
that infamous alternate ending going to come

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.480
into play?

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.400
What megastar is joining Smith?

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.460
All that and more, right here!

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.280
In 2007, Will Smith once again cemented his
place as one of Hollywood's most charismatic

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.449
movie stars when he played the lead in "I
Am Legend."

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:21.539
The film takes place in a post-apocalyptic
world where most humans have either been wiped

00:00:21.539 --> 00:00:25.130
out or turned into vampiric mutants known
as Darkseekers.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:29.899
"I Am Legend" follows the efforts of Smith's
Dr. Robert Neville, the sole human living

00:00:29.899 --> 00:00:34.400
in an overrun Manhattan, as he tries to find
a cure for the disease that changed the world

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.290
and, hopefully, link up with other human survivors.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.030
The movie is a loose adaptation of the 1954
Richard Matheson novel of the same name.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:47.230
"I Am Legend" was a box office success when
it was released in December 2007, earning

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.100
over $585 million worldwide, according to
BoxOfficeMojo.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:57.500
Plus, it received generally positive reviews
from both critics and casual moviegoers alike.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.920
Now, over a decade after the first film's
release, Will Smith is set to star in an "I

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.630
Am Legend" sequel, and he isn't the only notable
actor attached to the project.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.859
In March 2022, Deadline reported that Smith
had signed on to star in and executive produce

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:13.560
a sequel to "I Am Legend."

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.719
Shortly after the report's release, Smith
seemingly confirmed the news on Instagram

00:01:17.719 --> 00:01:22.390
when he posted an image of the post-apocalyptic
version of Manhattan from the first film.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.640
In addition to Smith, the sequel will also
star "Black Panther" and "Creed" actor Michael

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.109
B. Jordan, who is set to executive produce
the film alongside his co-star.

00:01:31.109 --> 00:01:36.909
Akiva Goldsman, who co-wrote the 2007 adaptation
of "I Am Legend," is set to write the sequel.

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:41.860
However, it's unclear if "I Am Legend" filmmaker
Francis Lawrence will return to helm the sequel,

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:46.829
or if it'll be another filmmaker who ultimately
sits in the director's seat for the follow-up.

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:50.799
The film's plot is similarly unknown right
now, and it does not currently have a set

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:51.799
release date.

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:56.009
Asked about the announcement in a recent interview
with Entertainment Tonight, Smith teased,

00:01:56.009 --> 00:01:57.579
"I can't talk about it yet.

00:01:57.579 --> 00:02:02.119
But it's a really, really cool concept and
[Michael B. Jordan] was a part of creating

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:03.179
the idea.

00:02:03.179 --> 00:02:05.360
[…] It was one of those [movies] I was gonna
leave alone."

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.470
Smith also admitted that he quickly reconsidered
once he heard the pitch for the sequel.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.990
As he told Entertainment Tonight, he remembers
thinking,

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.060
"'But that might work.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:14.860
I think we can do that.'"

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.780
With two massive stars like Jordan and Smith
attached to the project, it seems safe to

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.440
assume that it won't take too long for more
updates and details to start surfacing about

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.800
"I Am Legend 2."

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.360
One of the updates that "I Am Legend" fans
are undoubtedly most curious about is how

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:33.050
Smith plans to appear in the upcoming film,
especially considering his character's apparent

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.390
death at the climax of the first movie.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:39.330
While no plot details about the film have
been released as yet, that leaves plenty of

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.380
room for speculation.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.320
"Just fishing in the dark son."

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.600
One potential answer could involve a mixture
of flashbacks and de-aging software to return

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.440
Dr. Neville back to his pre-apocalyptic or
mid-apocalyptic image.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.590
There likely remains plenty of story to be
told about the immediate three years after

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.570
the outbreak of the Krippin Virus.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:03.770
Of course, Smith is no stranger to Hollywood's
de-aging practices as a result of his role

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:08.470
in 2019's "Gemini Man," a film which sees
Smith's character battle a younger version

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:09.470
of himself.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:13.410
Admittedly, however, this might be one of
the more predictable avenues writers could

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.410
employ.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.650
Another possible route that returns Dr. Neville
to the big screen involves an alternate ending

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.080
to the original 2007 film.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:25.560
The theatrical cut of "I Am Legend" sees Dr.
Neville sacrifice himself in order to save

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.610
a cure for the future of mankind.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:32.930
On its face, this scene is extremely unambiguous,
and by the end of the theatrical cut, Dr.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.310
Neville is dead.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.640
However, ardent fans of the film will also
surely remember an alternate ending included

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.230
on the DVD release.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.830
In addition to proving popular online, the
alternate ending is noted for its closer dedication

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.490
to the source material.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:50.530
Instead of concluding with a dramatic sacrifice,
this ending presents Dr. Neville with the

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:55.420
opportunity to make peace with the Darkseekers
he has been trying to "cure" for so long.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.620
Realizing that his experiments have instead
made him the monster, Dr. Neville abandons

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.360
his research and home.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.900
Making peace with his new reality, Dr. Neville
instead opts to join a group of human survivors

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:06.900
in Vermont.

